From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11, dxgi: textures shared between devices, keyed mutex rules, ClearView

OpenSharedResource and IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle were E_NOTIMPL, and the keyed
mutex of the previous work only ordered the users of one device.

 - A texture created with D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED or ..._SHARED_KEYEDMUTEX gets a
   legacy shared handle (a number no handle table knows: it cannot be duplicated or
   closed), IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle returns it (NULL for a resource that is not
   shared, E_INVALIDARG for NT handle sharing), and ID3D11Device::OpenSharedResource
   of another device of the process opens the same resource (OpenSharedResource1 refuses
   a legacy handle with E_INVALIDARG).
 - The devices share the mutex state. Acquiring a mutex the device holds, and releasing
   one the device does not hold, are DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL; a mutex whose holder is
   destroyed is abandoned (WAIT_ABANDONED for every later acquire). The pixels go with
   the key: ReleaseSync copies the texture out, AcquireSync into the texture. A shared
   texture without a keyed mutex shows what its maker had drawn when it was opened.
 - Sharing flags that make no sense are invalid: both kinds, an NT handle alone, any
   sharing below feature level 10.
 - ID3D11DeviceContext1::ClearView clears render target views (the given rectangles or
   the whole view) and unordered access views.
The matching todo_wine marks of the tests are removed. Sharing between processes and NT
handles remain unimplemented.
